    "blurb": "Update parameters on user tasks",
    "overview": "Update the priority, due date, follow-up date, assignment, and candidates of one or several user tasks in a running process instance.",
    "rating": null,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "mobileBundleId": null,
    "mobileAppStoreId": null
  },
  "overview": {
    "splashTitle": "Adjust user tasks automatically as processes run",
    "splashDescription": "User tasks that stay unassigned, overdue, or low priority can stall a process and slow down the people waiting on the result. The User Task Update Connector updates one or several user tasks of a process instance, including priority, due date, follow-up date, assignment (set an assignee or unassign), candidate groups, and candidate users. For example, when a timer fires, you can raise the priority of a user task, move its due date, force a new candidate list, or unassign the user if the task has been assigned for too long. This keeps work moving and puts tasks in front of the right people without manual intervention.",
    "imageUrl": "https://d3bql97l1ytoxn.cloudfront.net/app_resources/873328/overview/img5009761678236657866.png?478bc3ef6cda292c5b7d5fdbb15c8bb9",
